// The join half of canon_body, split out so that canon_body has an action to
// spend on dropping `blank` nodes first.
//
// The split is here rather than at the five call sites because `id` forbids a
// call inside a call's argument: canon_body(blank_drop(x)) is illegal, so
// filtering outside would cost every caller a named intermediate, and four of
// the five callers are already at the action limit.

canon_join(int[] stmts) {
  string out = "";
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len(stmts)) {
    out = out + sep_at(";", i) + canon_stmt(stmts[i]);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return string out;
given elif_fixture ((import no_stmts)):("")
given canon_begun_fixture ((import lz_body1)):("d:int 0=I3;e:c(foo:I3)")

// A `blank` statement and a list holding one, for the filter cst4 and
// blank_drop exist for. Nothing else in the tree builds a node of that kind:
// parse_blank (front/parse/stmt/form/more.id) is the only constructor, and it
// takes a token cursor, so the leaf is built the same way here.
// lz_g's program with a canonicalisation begun over it. Every statement form
// below decl reaches cn() for a local name, which reads the position map that
// only uq_begin exports -- and no lz_* fixture runs it, because the loose
// canonicaliser calls uq_begin itself from lz_func.
canon_begun_fixture() {
  lz_g();
  uq_begin("f");
} return void;
